{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Put every event a tracker tracks in a session, and sample whole sessions."}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Putting events in sessions","anchor":"Putting-events-in-sessions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(timeout:kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEventKind","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/NonPositiveSessionTimeout"]},{"title":"Reading a record’s session","anchor":"Reading-a-records-session","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey"]},{"title":"Session events","anchor":"Session-events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"]},{"title":"Sampling whole sessions","anchor":"Sampling-whole-sessions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Trackers\/Sampler\/sessions(where:rate:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sessions are opt-in. Add the sessions enricher to the ones a tracker is built with, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s worker sets each record’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to its session’s identifier. A session goes on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while each event comes less than the timeout (30 minutes by default) after the one before it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured between the records’ timestamps. The first event after a longer gap starts a new session."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The enricher tracks "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" before each session’s first event, and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before that from the second session on, carrying the ended session’s duration. A run’s last session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has no "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": a session ends only when an event comes after the timeout. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kinds:"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"track only one kind of session event, or neither; every record still carries its key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session’s identifier is a version 7 UUID: the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, then random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bits. It is held in the enricher’s memory only, never written to disk, and a new tracker, as on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next launch, starts a new session. Records a store kept from an earlier run carry no key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its session events with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, by the record’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It needs the sessions enricher among the tracker’s enrichers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For the app, device, operating system, locale and network an event was tracked on, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"StandardContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For the app’s opens and moves to the background, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"LifecycleTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its ","type":"text"},{"code":"ApplicationOpened","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after a long time in the background starts a new session here, though","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither module knows about the other.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Sessions","import Trackers","","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [try .sessions(timeout: .seconds(15 * 60), kinds: [.started])])","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))  \/\/ tracks SessionStarted, then SignedUp, both with the same SessionKey"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers sessions beside the standard context, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers sampling.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"Sessions","modules":[{"name":"Sessions"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"Sessions"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/sessions"]}],"references":{"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions/Events/Enricher/sessions(timeout:kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/s